# An operator asks for a cut verification that stops at its first red, and is
# refused before any work.
#
# A piece (`part <i> of <n>`) is dealt so debt clearing proves every stage in
# it. A piece that stopped early would leave stages of it unproven while
# reading as the piece that was asked for, so `first-red` with `part` is
# refused with exit 2, the reason, and the two spellings that work: first-red
# over the whole population, or every stage of one piece.
#
# The fixture runs the real `le verify worktree` action against a throwaway
# checkout (ZE_REPO_ROOT), so a refusal that broke would start a worktree there
# and never in the shared tree. Delete the check in Options.part
# (internal/le/verify/lifecycle.go, firstRedWithPart) and seq=1 fails.

option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture runner/verify-first-red-refuses-a-cut
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=first-red-with-part-refused
expect=stdout:contains=no-worktree-created
